{"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/privacymanifests"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"title":"Privacy Manifests"},"abstract":[{"text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Choosing-what-to-record","title":"Choosing what to record"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Traffluent collects nothing on its own. It records only the events your app tracks and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context your app turns on: every kind of automatic instrumentation and every standard enricher is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"opt in. It sends records only to the destinations your app gives a delivery, to endpoints your app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names. None of it is used for tracking as Apple defines it: no module links what it records with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other companies’ data, reads the advertising identifier, fingerprints the device, or works around"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the user’s consent or App Tracking Transparency. Every manifest declares "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyTracking"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" and lists no tracking domains."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each module that can produce data of one of Apple’s collected data types ships a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" declaring it. SwiftPM and Bazel both put it in a resource bundle named","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Traffluent_<Module>.bundle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which Xcode and rules_apple copy into your app, where Xcode’s privacy","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"report finds it. A module your app doesn’t link adds nothing to the report.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Required-reason-APIs","text":"Required-reason APIs","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No Traffluent module calls an API on Apple’s list of required-reason APIs, so every manifest’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty. The list’s categories are file timestamps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp"},{"type":"text","text":"), system boot time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime"},{"type":"text","text":"), disk space"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace"},{"type":"text","text":"), active keyboards"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryActiveKeyboards"},{"type":"text","text":") and user defaults"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults"},{"type":"text","text":"). The modules that come nearest:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Module","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"What it calls","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why none is a required-reason API"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"swift-system’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileDescriptor"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"open"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"read"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seek"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"resize"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close"},{"text":"), ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unlink"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileManager"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"createDirectory"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setAttributes"},{"text":" (the file protection class), ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contentsOfDirectory"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isExcludedFromBackup"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It reads no file’s timestamps, size from "},{"code":"stat","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or the volume’s free space: a segment’s size is the offset "},{"code":"seek","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" returns at its end, and the store bounds itself by the bytes it has written."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileManager.fileExists"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data(contentsOf:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data.write(to:options:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileVersionStore"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProcessInfo.performExpiringActivity"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It reads and writes the version file’s contents, never its attributes."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"sysctlbyname","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for ","type":"text"},{"code":"hw.machine","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"hw.model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ProcessInfo.operatingSystemVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Bundle.infoDictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Locale.current","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"NWPathMonitor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"identifierForVendor","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None is on the list; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.vendorIdentifier()"},{"type":"text","text":" is declared as collected data below."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The tracker’s record timestamps (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A session’s inactivity is measured between records’